---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
---

<Base
  title="About Us"
  description="Students 2 Science (S2S) inspires and empowers students through hands-on STEM learning. Learn who we are, what we do, and why this site exists."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="hero__tag">
        <span aria-hidden="true">●</span> About Us
      </span>
      <h1>We empower students to succeed with STEM</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Students 2 Science (S2S) is a New Jersey nonprofit that brings real
        science, real labs and real scientists to students - many of them from
        communities that have never had that chance.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <h2>Our mission</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        To inspire and empower all students through hands-on learning
        experiences, encouraging them to pursue careers in science,
        technology, engineering and math - and in doing so, to strengthen the
        future workforce.
      </p>

      <h2>Our vision</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Every student in New Jersey should have access to STEM learning
        opportunities and career pathways. That means:
      </p>
      <ul class="muted">
        <li>Expanding our programs to reach 450,000 students every year.</li>
        <li>Operating 3-5 Technology Centers in the areas that need them most.</li>
        <li>
          Building curriculum that matches what the state's future workforce
          will actually require.
        </li>
        <li>
          Giving students the room to explore and define their own STEM career
          and education pathways.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our impact</h2>
      <p>
        Since 2009, hands-on STEM experiences, innovative programming,
        state-of-the-art Technology Centers and direct work with professional
        scientists have reached students, communities and the economy:
      </p>
      <div class="impact-grid">
        <article class="card card--flat">
          <h3 class="card__title">Individuals</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            More than 500,000 students in New Jersey need education support,
            especially in STEM. S2S opens that door: to date, our programs have
            served over 300,000 students with immersive, hands-on experiences
            using real laboratory instrumentation.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card card--flat">
          <h3 class="card__title">Communities</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            Many of our students come from communities that lack the experts,
            resources and facilities high-quality STEM education needs. S2S
            gives them critical skills and mentoring - the kind that can lift
            an entire community.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card card--flat">
          <h3 class="card__title">The economy</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            The Bureau of Labor Statistics projects STEM jobs will grow 10.4%
            between 2023 and 2033 - nearly three times faster than non-STEM
            jobs. S2S is preparing students to fill those well-paid roles.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <h2>Achievement highlights</h2>
      <ul class="muted">
        <li>Engaged over 350,000 students in S2S programs.</li>
        <li>Established two state-of-the-art Technology Centers.</li>
        <li>
          Created a formal partnership with Newark Public Schools, New
          Jersey's largest school district.
        </li>
        <li>
          Partnered with more than 200 schools and community organizations
          across New Jersey and beyond.
        </li>
        <li>
          Involved over 1,000 corporate, higher education and community
          volunteers.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>About this site</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        STEM Pathways is built by Students 2 Science. Every salary, job count
        and growth figure comes from official government sources - see
        <a href={withBase('/sources')}>where the data comes from</a>. Want to
        see how a lab experiment connects to a real career? Start with
        <a href={withBase('/labs2life')}>Labs2Life</a>. Curious about our work
        with high school students? Read about the
        <a href={withBase('/cap-program')}>Career Advancement Program</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .impact-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-s);
    margin-block: var(--space-m);
  }
  @media (min-width: 46rem) {
    .impact-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
